A shared include supplies a dependency whose config_path is resolved from
each including unit's directory (get_terragrunt_dir() is the child's) to a
directory that does not exist. GRT002 is attributed to the including unit,
so two including units give two diagnostics at the same file:line:col in
the include. The include file itself is not a unit.
-- _envcommon/db.hcl --
dependency "vpc" {
  config_path = "${get_terragrunt_dir()}/../vpc"
}
-- live/app1/terragrunt.hcl --
include "db" {
  path = find_in_parent_folders("_envcommon/db.hcl")
}

inputs = {}
-- live/app2/terragrunt.hcl --
include "db" {
  path = find_in_parent_folders("_envcommon/db.hcl")
}

inputs = {}
-- _golden/exit --
1
-- _golden/want --
# _envcommon/db.hcl line 2: "  config_path = " is 16 bytes.
GRT002 error _envcommon/db.hcl:2:17 live/app1
GRT002 error _envcommon/db.hcl:2:17 live/app2
-- _golden/messages --
GRT002 _envcommon/db.hcl:2:17 dependency "vpc" config_path resolves to "live/vpc": directory does not exist
GRT002 _envcommon/db.hcl:2:17 dependency "vpc" config_path resolves to "live/vpc": directory does not exist
